      {
        "text": "British Galleries:\nEmbroidered screens were popular Arts and Crafts furnishings.  This example by Morris & Company was designed by John Henry Dearle, William Morris's assistant, and embroidered under the supervision of William's daughter May Morris, who ran the Embroidery Section of the firm. These panels were also available for sale  in kit form to embroider at home.",
